  "body": "## What\n\n`crates/app/src/stock_play.rs` (`FieldPlay`, `PlayIndex`) and `crates/app/src/stock_play_worker.rs` (`PlayWorker`) hold domain logic. They cut the stock and serve the playback pictures. Only `PlaySeed::gather` and `FieldPlay::new` read the ECS world.\n\nAGENTS.md \"app holds the document, nothing else\" puts this code in the simulation crate.\n\n## Context\n\nThe review of PR #2192 (issue #2181) found the same rule for the new keyframe code. That PR moved the keyframe store and the calculation loop to `camcraft_sim::play_keys` and `camcraft_sim::play_precalc`. The methods of `FieldPlay` and `PlayWorker` stayed in app, because these types are in app. They existed before #2181.\n\n## Done means\n\n- `FieldPlay`, `PlayIndex`, `PlayWorker` and their head and precalc methods are in `camcraft-sim`.\n- `PlaySeed::gather` (the world read) stays in app. App re-exports the moved items.\n- The rotary and lathe cut helpers that `FieldPlay::cut` calls are reachable from sim, or are passed in.\n- The playback suites (`stock_play`, `stock_play_partial`, `stock_play_precalc`, `stock_view`) pass unchanged.\n- No change to the picture, the Deviate verdict or the post gate.\n",
